          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A <strong class="text-white">stainless steel humidifier</strong> earns its premium in one way: the tank stays smooth, clean and easy to sanitize through years of scrubbing and dishwasher cycles, where plastic slowly scratches and clouds. It does not prevent mold, it does not stop white dust, and most of the other wet parts are still plastic.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy one if you will clean it every week and want that job to be fast, and pair it with distilled water. If you have hard water or know your routine will slip, a well-designed plastic ultrasonic or an evaporative humidifier will serve you better for less money.
          </p>
